{"async on forEach callback is now a no-op and misleading - the async keyword on remindersToUpdate.forEach callback is vestigial since nothing inside is awaited, and forEach does not await async callbacks": 0.21088752150535583, "immediateDelete path cancels via SendGrid but never deletes the DB record - when immediateDelete is true and referenceId is non-null, the function posts cancellation to SendGrid and returns without deleting the WorkflowReminder row from the database": 0.9586693644523621, "Null referenceId will cause a failed SendGrid request - remindersToCancel query does not filter for referenceId IS NOT NULL, and passing batch_id: null to POST /v3/user/scheduled_sends will result in a SendGrid API error that aborts the for loop": 0.9861667156219482, "Single try/catch around the entire loop aborts on the first failure - if client.request throws for any reminder, control jumps to catch block and any pending prisma.workflowReminder.delete operations already pushed are never awaited": 0.9937829375267029, "Missing method filter causes wrong API calls for non-email reminders - remindersToCancel query has no method: WorkflowMethods.EMAIL filter, so non-email reminders with cancelled: true would have their Twilio SID passed as batch_id to SendGrid API": 0.9881399869918823, "unscheduledReminders query should exclude cancelled reminders defensively - query fetches reminders with scheduled: false but does not exclude records where cancelled: true, which could cause re-scheduling of reminders for cancelled bookings": 0.802073061466217}